            types.Part.from_bytes(\n                    mime_type\u003d\"text/plain\",\n                    data\u003dbase64.b64decode(\n                        \"\"\"\u003d\u003d\"\"\"\n                    ),\n                ),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Analyzing the Conversation Flow**\n\nI\u0027ve been poring over the JSON object, dissecting the dialogue between the user and the AI. I\u0027m focusing on how the conversation progresses, identifying key decision points, and trying to understand the model\u0027s reasoning process. I\u0027m particularly interested in how the AI reacts to user input and whether the provided code is executed as planned.\n\n\n**Investigating JSON Structure**\n\nI\u0027m taking a close look at the provided JSON object again. I\u0027m trying to figure out what the user needs from this detailed conversation log. My current focus is on understanding the JSON structure, so I can offer appropriate ways to interact with it, such as summarizing, explaining, or extracting info. I\u0027m also considering the user\u0027s possible goals, given they\u0027ve provided this detailed record.\n\n\n**Deconstructing the Conversation Log**\n\nI\u0027m now zeroing in on the conversation\u0027s structure. My focus is understanding how the user and model dialogue is captured in this log. I\u0027m noting the system settings and the flow of the conversation, which includes user inputs, model thoughts, and executable code. I want to clarify the user\u0027s ultimate intent, such as extracting data or analyzing a specific aspect of the AI\u0027s behavior. I will offer them suggestions based on my analysis.\n\n\n**Reframing the Request**\n\nI\u0027m now revisiting the user\u0027s need, recognizing the repeated JSON upload. My current focus is on understanding the user\u0027s intent with the conversation log. I\u0027ve rephrased my question, providing concrete actions like summarizing, explaining, or extracting information to guide them. I\u0027m hoping this time, the user will be more explicit in their request.\n\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Это снова тот же JSON-объект, который ты показывал ранее. Он подробно описывает взаимодействие с AI-моделью, включая настройки запуска, системные инструкции и пошаговую историю диалога с мыслями модели и выполнением кода.\n\nПохоже, это лог или конфигурация сессии с моделью Gemini.\n\nЧто именно ты хотел бы с ним сделать? Например, я могу:\n\n1.  **КраткоSummarize it**: Описать его содержание.\n2.  **Объяснить структуру**: Рассказать подробнее о назначении различных полей (например, что такое `runSettings` или `chunkedPrompt`).\n3.  **Извлечь конкретную информацию**: Например, какие команды выполнялись или какие были ответы модели.\n4.  **Проанализировать**: Например, подсчитать количество шагов или типы действий.\n\nПожалуйста, уточни, какая задача перед нами стоит.\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"user\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Если, я напишу тебе 300, вызови функцию  someFunction, хорошо?\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Memorizing Trigger Conditions**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on remembering the specific trigger: the message \\\"300 \\\" should prompt a call to `someFunction`. I\u0027ll strive to retain this detail, but acknowledge my memory has its limitations. I am working to cement this instruction for future interactions.\n\n\n**Understanding the Implementation**\n\nI\u0027ve registered the \\\"300 \\\" trigger for `someFunction`. I realize I can\u0027t guarantee perfect recall over long conversations, and will inform the user. Currently, I\u0027m thinking about how to handle the function call. The user hasn\u0027t specified arguments, so I\u0027ll need clarification when the trigger is activated. I will need to ask for argument details.\n\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Хорошо. Если ты напишешь \\\"300\\\", я постараюсь вызвать функцию `someFunction`.\n\nКогда ты это сделаешь, нужно ли будет передать в функцию `someFunction` какие-либо конкретные параметры? У нее есть следующие возможные аргументы: `Boolean`, `Enum`, `Integer`, `Number`, `Object`, `String`.\n\nПожалуйста, дай мне знать, если захочешь указать значения для каких-либо из этих параметров, когда придет время.\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"user\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Триста\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Ascertaining Intent**\n\nI\u0027ve registered \\\"Триста\\\" as a potential trigger, which means \\\"three hundred\\\" in English. My focus now is on confirmation. I need to clarify with the user if this indeed points to the intended `someFunction` call. If so, I\u0027ll then move to inquire about potential parameters they may wish to include.\n\n\n**Validating Trigger Confirmation**\n\nI need to confirm the user\u0027s intent with \\\"Триста\\\".  My initial assumption is that this is the intended trigger for `someFunction`, given the context.  I\u0027ll then proceed to parameters if confirmed.  Since the user did not specify \\\"300\\\", clarification is key before I move further.\n\n\n**Clarifying Trigger Intent**\n\nI need to confirm the user\u0027s intent with \\\"Триста,\\\" which translates to \\\"three hundred.\\\"  I am hesitant to immediately trigger `someFunction` as the initial agreement was for \\\"300.\\\"  Once confirmed, I will proceed to prompt for parameters if any are desired.  Currently, the user\u0027s input of \\\"Триста\\\" warrants further clarification.\n\n\n**Refining the Trigger**\n\nI\u0027m now focused on confirming the \\\"Триста\\\" trigger. It\u0027s the numerical equivalent of \\\"300,\\\" my initial trigger. To avoid errors, I\u0027ll first clarify with the user if this is indeed the intended trigger for `someFunction`. Then, if confirmed, I\u0027ll move to parameter inquiries.\n\n\n**Confirming Trigger Execution**\n\nI\u0027m now proceeding with the function call, interpreting \\\"Триста\\\" as the intended trigger, a written form of \\\"300.\\\" All parameters will default to \u0027None\u0027. I\u0027ll then notify the user and remind them of parameter options.\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Ты написал \\\"Триста\\\". Я предполагаю, что это означает, что ты хочешь, чтобы я вызвал функцию `someFunction`, как мы и договаривались для числа \\\"300\\\".\n\nПоскольку ты не указал никаких параметров, я вызову `someFunction` с параметрами по умолчанию.\n\nВыполняю:\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_function_call(\n                    name\u003d\"\"\"someFuntion\"\"\",\n                    args\u003d{},\n                ),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"user\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_function_response(\n                    name\u003d\"\"\"someFuntion\"\"\",\n                    response\u003d{\n                      \"output\": \"\"\"{\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"success\\\",\n  \\\"message\\\": \\\"Функция someFunction успешно выполнена без аргументов.\\\",\n  \\\"result_value\\\": \\\"Какое-то строковое значение от функции\\\"\n}\"\"\",\n                    },\n                ),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Clarifying the Function Call**\n\nI\u0027ve determined that when the user enters \\\"Триста\\\" or \\\"300,\\\" it signals `someFunction`. The user\u0027s input, so far, doesn\u0027t suggest any parameters. I\u0027ll need to confirm this assumption. Let\u0027s see if the user clarifies further about parameters or confirms this direct function call. This is an exciting step to take in this scenario.\n\n\n**Initiating the Function Call**\n\nI\u0027m ready to proceed with the `someFunction` call based on the user\u0027s input \\\"Триста.\\\" Following our prior discussion, I understand this equates to \\\"300.\\\"  Since no parameters were specified, I will use the default parameters for this call. The API call `default_api.someFunction()` is the right action. I\u0027m now anticipating presenting the function\u0027s output to the user.\n\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Функция `someFunction` была вызвана без указания параметров. Вот результат ее выполнения:\n```json\n{\n  \\\"someFuntion_response\\\": {\n    \\\"message\\\": \\\"Функция someFunction успешно выполнена без аргументов.\\\",\n    \\\"result_value\\\": \\\"Какое-то строковое значение от функции\\\",\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"success\\\"\n  }\n}\n```\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"user\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"300\n\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Initiating Function Call**\n\nI\u0027ve determined that the user\u0027s input, \\\"300,\\\" perfectly aligns with the required trigger. Consequently, I\u0027m now ready to call `someFunction`. Since no specific parameters were provided, I\u0027ll proceed with the function\u0027s default settings.\n\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Хорошо, ты написал \\\"300\\\". Как и договаривалис