from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"300, добавь параметры вызова, q\u003d\\\"ok?\\\"\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Exploring Function Parameters**\n\nI\u0027m now considering the available parameters for `someFunction`. It seems the intention is to pass a parameter, specifically `q\u003d\\\"ok?\\\"`. However, looking at the function\u0027s definition, the accepted parameters are `bool` and a Literal type. I need to figure out how to reconcile this discrepancy and if a type conversion is needed.\n\n\n**Clarifying Parameter Intent**\n\nI\u0027m now focused on understanding the user\u0027s intent with the parameter `q\u003d\\\"ok?\\\"`. It seems the user believes `q` is a valid parameter name, but it isn\u0027t defined as such. I\u0027m considering the possibility that \\\"ok?\\\" is meant for the `String` parameter. To ensure clarity and adhere to API constraints, I need to confirm if the user intends to set the `String` parameter to \\\"ok?\\\" or if `q` is a placeholder for a different parameter name. I should re-evaluate the user\u0027s initial prompt in the context of our recent exchange.\n\n\n**Identifying Invalid Parameters**\n\nI\u0027ve examined the user\u0027s intent more closely. The directive to add the parameter `q\u003d\u0027ok?\u0027` raises a red flag.  The function documentation doesn\u0027t list `q` as a valid parameter. I\u0027m now certain the user believes `q` is valid. My revised approach will acknowledge their request, inform them about the invalid parameter name, and offer the valid parameter list for review. I\u0027ll then proactively suggest an alternative parameter, like `String`, if the user intended to pass a string value.\n\n\n**Refining Response Strategy**\n\nI\u0027m now finalizing the response to the user\u0027s request. Based on their input \\\"q\u003d\u0027ok?\u0027\\\", I\u0027ll acknowledge the call to `someFunction`, inform them that `q` is not a valid parameter, and provide a list of available parameters. Following this, I\u0027ll suggest using the `String` parameter with the value \\\"ok?\\\" if that was their intent. This approach prioritizes accurate information and user assistance. I\u0027m confident in the effectiveness of my tailored response.\n\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Ты написал \\\"300\\\", и хочешь вызвать `someFunction`. Ты также указал параметр `q\u003d\\\"ok?\\\"`.\n\nОднако у функции `someFunction` нет параметра с именем `q`. Доступные параметры для `someFunction`:\n*   `Boolean` (логический тип)\n*   `Enum` (перечисление: \u0027value_1\u0027 или \u0027value_N\u0027)\n*   `Integer` (целое число)\n*   `Number` (число)\n*   `Object` (объект)\n*   `String` (строка)\n\nВозможно, ты хотел использовать строковый параметр `String` со значением \\\"ok?\\\" ? Если да, я могу вызвать функцию так: `someFunction(String\u003d\\\"ok?\\\")`.\n\nКак бы ты хотел поступить?\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"user\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"300, Boolean\u003dtrue\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Executing the Function Call**\n\nI\u0027m ready to execute `default_api.someFuntion ` now. I\u0027ve successfully interpreted the user\u0027s intent and will be passing `True` as the Boolean value. My next step will be to confirm the function call was successful.\n\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Отлично! Ты написал \\\"300\\\" и указал параметр `Boolean\u003dtrue`.\n\nВызываю `someFunction` с этим параметром:\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_function_call(\n                    name\u003d\"\"\"someFuntion\"\"\",\n                    args\u003d{\"Boolean\":true},\n                ),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"user\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_function_response(\n                    name\u003d\"\"\"someFuntion\"\"\",\n                    response\u003d{\n                      \"output\": \"\"\"{\n  \\\"status_code\\\": 200,\n  \\\"numeric_result\\\": 12345\n}\"\"\",\n                    },\n                ),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"model\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"**Considering the Boolean**\n\nI\u0027ve acknowledged the call to `someFunction` with a true Boolean. Now, I\u0027m waiting to see the results. I\u0027m focusing on the outcome from this specific condition. I\u0027ll provide an update when I have the result.\n\n\n\"\"\"),\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"Функция `someFunction` была вызвана с параметром `Boolean\u003dTrue`. Вот результат ее выполнения:\n\n```json\n{\n  \\\"someFuntion_response\\\": {\n    \\\"numeric_result\\\": 12345,\n    \\\"status_code\\\": 200\n  }\n}\n```\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n        types.Content(\n            role\u003d\"user\",\n            parts\u003d[\n                types.Part.from_text(text\u003d\"\"\"INSERT_INPUT_HERE\"\"\"),\n            ],\n        ),\n    ]\n    tools \u003d [\n        types.Tool(\n            function_declarations\u003d[\n                types.FunctionDeclaration(\n                    name\u003d\"someFuntion\",\n                    description\u003d\"Description\",\n                    parameters\u003dgenai.types.Schema(\n                        type \u003d genai.types.Type.OBJECT,\n                        properties \u003d {\n                            \"String\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                type \u003d genai.types.Type.STRING,\n                            ),\n                            \"Number\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                type \u003d genai.types.Type.NUMBER,\n                            ),\n                            \"Integer\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                type \u003d genai.types.Type.INTEGER,\n                            ),\n                            \"Boolean\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                type \u003d genai.types.Type.BOOLEAN,\n                            ),\n                            \"Object\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                type \u003d genai.types.Type.OBJECT,\n                                properties \u003d {\n                                    \"String\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                        type \u003d genai.types.Type.STRING,\n                                    ),\n                                    \"Number\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                        type \u003d genai.types.Type.NUMBER,\n                                    ),\n                                    \"Integer\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                        type \u003d genai.types.Type.INTEGER,\n                                    ),\n                                    \"Bollean\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                        type \u003d genai.types.Type.BOOLEAN,\n                                    ),\n                                    \"ОJbject\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                        type \u003d genai.types.Type.OBJECT,\n                                        properties \u003d {\n                                            \"String\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                                type \u003d genai.types.Type.STRING,\n                                            ),\n                                            \"Number\": genai.types.Schema(\n                                                type \u003d genai.types.Type.NUMBER,\n                      